1. Work performed: Added reusable NVFP4 packing via `DeviceNvfp4Matrix::PackInto` in [device_nvfp4_matrix.h](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/include/nemotron/device_nvfp4_matrix.h#L41) and [device_nvfp4_matrix.cu](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/device_nvfp4_matrix.cu#L349). It validates shape/layout, runs the existing four pack kernels into pre-allocated buffers, and refreshes the cached host tensor scale after each pack. `PackDeviceRowMajorFp32ToNvfp4()` now just allocates once and delegates to `PackInto`. In [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L769) and [expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L1581), `ExpertLayerSlice::Impl` now pre-allocates `normalized_pack` `[1, hidden_size]`, `routed_activated_pack` `[1, routed_expert_intermediate_size]`, and `shared_activated_pack` `[1, shared_expert_intermediate_size]`, and the direct cuBLASLt MoE path reuses them with `PackInto` instead of per-call `DeviceNvfp4Matrix` creation ([expert_layer.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/expert_layer.cpp#L864)). In [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L23) and [linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L357), `UploadedLinearOp::Impl` now pre-allocates one `[1, input_cols]` activation pack for NVFP4 ops and reuses it for `token_count==1`; the `token_count>1` path still uses the existing allocation flow ([linear_op.cpp](/home/khkramer/src/nemotron-inference/runtime/src/backend/linear_op.cpp#L513)).

2. Compile status: `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target nemotron_runtime_backend -j4` passed. `cmake --build build-phase1-tests --target full_forward_manifest_smoke_test -j4` passed. `git diff --check` on the touched files passed.

3. Any concerns: No compile issues remain. The reusable pack buffers are mutable per-instance scratch, so they rely on the same single in-flight use model already assumed by the existing decode scratch buffers. `runtime/src/backend/nvfp4_gemm_runner.cpp` did not need changes because the multi-token path intentionally stays on the current allocation-based fallback.

